      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dynamic strain aging controls the temperature- and strain-rate-dependent mechanical behavior of FeNiCrMn.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At intermediate temperatures, increased atomic mobility enables dynamic interactions between constituent solutes and moving dislocations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interactions of Fe, Ni, Cr, and Mn atoms with moving dislocations cause temporary dislocation pinning.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Temporary solute-mediated dislocation pinning constitutes dynamic strain aging.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dynamic strain aging increases work hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dynamic strain aging delays plastic instability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Solute-dislocation pinning can enhance both strength and ductility in the intermediate-temperature regime.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At intermediate temperatures and moderate strain rates, yield strength will be anomalously higher than at approximately 300 K and 10^-3 s^-1.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At intermediate temperatures and moderate strain rates, strain hardening will be enhanced relative to the room-temperature baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted increases in yield strength and strain hardening produce an improved strength-ductility balance.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dynamic-strain-aging effect diminishes at temperatures below or above the intermediate regime.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant intermediate regime activates atomic diffusion without creep becoming dominant.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism applies specifically to as-solidified, single-phase FeNiCrMn solid-solution microstructures.",
